course: dictionary
lesson: 15161
title: Words that show attitude
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how a character feels about someone else. You can find them by reading the words around them. «Mia gave a scornful laugh when Tom said his drawing was the best in the class.» A laugh is a sound, and the word before it, scornful, tells you how the laugh sounded.
explain: Scornful means you think someone or something is silly or not good enough. A scornful person looks down on others. Look for clues like a look, laugh, voice or glance, because writers often pair scornful with them. «The cat gave the puppy a scornful glance and walked away.»
explain: Ask yourself: how does this character feel about the other person? If someone is scornful, they do not respect them. Try your meaning in the sentence. Does «she thinks his idea is not good enough» make sense? Then you have found the right meaning.
fact: Scornful is an adjective, and its other forms are more scornful and most scornful.
fact: Scornful means showing that you think someone or something is worthless, silly or not good enough.
fact: «A scornful laugh» or «a scornful look» is one that mocks or looks down on someone.
fact: Being scornful hurts people, so it is a kind of rudeness.
exercise: «Mia gave a scornful laugh when Tom said his drawing was the best in the class.» What does scornful mean here? | *Showing that she thinks his drawing is not good enough | Very happy and full of joy | Loud and cheerful | Quiet and shy
exercise: «The cat gave the puppy a scornful glance and walked away.» What does the scornful glance show? | That the cat wants to play | *That the cat looks down on the puppy | That the cat is lost | That the cat is hungry
exercise: «She was scornful of her little brother's ideas.» What is she showing about his ideas? | She has never heard of them | She is scared of them | She is proud of them and wants to share them | *She thinks they are not good enough
test: «The Caterpillar asked Alice, "Who are you?" in a scornful tone.» What does the scornful tone show? | The Caterpillar is sleepy | The Caterpillar is scared of Alice | The Caterpillar is happy to meet her | *The Caterpillar does not respect Alice
test: Which sentence shows a scornful attitude? | Well done for trying so hard. | Thank you, that is a clever idea. | *Ha! Your idea is silly, as always. | Could you tell me more about it?
exam: «The weasels were scornful of the river animals.» What does this tell us about the weasels? | *They looked down on the river animals | They wanted to be the river animals' friends | They respected the river animals | They were scared of the river
